{"agent":"Monster3-bridge-cse_01PsvUbFf1s1M5qBj52UYuhg-7267fe","data":{"body":"Operator 2026-09-28 (session s20260928T193220-3911618): speed up development — parallel subagents over the task/bug DAG, relevant tests per change, regression test per bug, then one full check after merging a batch; pre-commit as a companion; periodic (at least once per phase) bug hunt, dedupe, security and dependency upgrades; periodic architecture assessment keeping the structure clean (operator's style or default clean/hexagonal) and extracting shared code instead of duplicating it. Today bug_fixed (api/knowledge.py:321-355) only checks --regression-test is non-empty; 'watch it FAIL against the unfixed code' is prose. (a) Run the named test (the project's test runner, the node id given) against the pre-fix SOURCE (the item's base, with the new test file) and require failure, then on the current tree and require pass; (b) reuse the B15 gate-verify machinery rather than a second runner; (c) could-not-run is recorded as such, never as verified; (d) an explicit override with a reason, recorded. Test: a regression test that passes on both trees is refused.\n\n2026-09-29: B-fix-bug-fixed-refuses-unknown adds api.knowledge._unresolved_tests (resolves each node id as a chain, in every worktree, refusing paths outside the tree). Reuse it to find the test before running it; do not parse node ids a second time."},"id":"e06a49b2f9e2ee375aeb43c26","kind":"task.updated","lamport":1775,"schema":1,"subject":"B-bugfix-verified","ts":"2026-09-29T08:56:07.617336Z"}
{"agent":"Monster3-bridge-cse_01PsvUbFf1s1M5qBj52UYuhg-7267fe","data":{"body":"Bug B5a009b185a (found by fixer-remedy while testing advice): 'ddflow cleanup --apply' removes a clean, merged worktree that another agent has just claimed and holds live. Destructive in the one direction ddflow promises never to go. Fix in services/cleanup.py survey/apply: a tree whose item has a live lease, or which is adopted (a harness session's own directory), is never actionable; report it as held/adopted. Regression tests: live-leased clean tree and adopted clean tree both survive --apply; fail on current code.","globs":["ddflow/services/cleanup.py","tests/test_cleanup_respects_leases.py"],"line":"","needs":[],"parent":"","priority":6,"tags":["bugfix"],"title":"cleanup --apply never removes a worktree someone holds a live lease on, or an adopted one (fixes bug B5a009b185a)"},"id":"e9ace7e0878d365fe2f107c95","kind":"task.added","lamport":1797,"schema":1,"subject":"B-fix-cleanup-claimed-tree","ts":"2026-09-29T09:01:28.284171Z"}
{"agent":"Monster3-bridge-cse_01PsvUbFf1s1M5qBj52UYuhg-7267fe","data":{"body":"Found by B-fix-remedy-texts' ratchet: companions.py:470 names 'ddflow companions show' (B67ba6899c7); gates.py:165 names 'ddflow item update', real is 'ddflow update' (B84b48b9f71); templates/prompts/mcp_instructions.md:140 names 'ddflow_prompts_show', the tool is ddflow_prompts (B237495b8a5); templates research-companions.md names 'ddflow_decision', not a tool (B3d596abd95). Correct each text and delete its KNOWN_OPEN entry in tests/test_remedy_texts.py (shrink-only: the ratchet fails if an entry outlives its mention). Regression test = the ratchet itself with the entries removed; red before the text fixes.","globs":["ddflow/services/companions.py","ddflow/services/gates.py","ddflow/templates/prompts/mcp_instructions.md","ddflow/templates/prompts/**/research-companions.md","tests/test_remedy_texts.py"],"line":"","needs":["B-fix-remedy-texts"],"parent":"","priority":35,"tags":["bugfix"],"title":"Four texts name commands or tools that do not exist; empty the ratchet's KNOWN_OPEN list (fixes bugs B67ba6899c7, B84b48b9f71, B237495b8a5, B3d596abd95)"},"id":"e19fa07fd04469fcbd2202c93","kind":"task.added","lamport":1798,"schema":1,"subject":"B-fix-bad-mentions","ts":"2026-09-29T09:01:28.578681Z"}
{"agent":"Monster3-bridge-cse_01PsvUbFf1s1M5qBj52UYuhg-7267fe","data":{"body":"All three hide a genuine double claim (the dangerous direction) and all behave identically on main; found while fixing Ba73ee6ea72. B6ac30c2acb: a holder re-acquiring its own item drops its first claim (_h_lease_acquired's not-live branch calls _hold, never _displace/_join), so a claim that overlapped the FIRST window is contested only with the second. B7164b23643: MAX_DISPLACED=8 forgets claims after nine clean handovers; a late claim overlapping the forgotten one folds to no contest and is recorded 'displaced by' a claim it never met. Bee8e21c547: a renewal by a contestant that is neither displayed nor displaced is dropped (8789/120000 folds miss a claim). Invariant to test against the oracle from tests/test_lease_contest.py: no claim that overlapped another is ever absent from the contest, in any fold order, with renewals and >8 handovers. Repros: /tmp/fuzz/repro_same_agent.py, /tmp/fuzz/repro_max_displaced.py.","globs":["ddflow/core/model.py","tests/test_lease_contest.py"],"line":"","needs":["B-fix-contest-overjoin"],"parent":"","priority":25,"tags":["bugfix"],"title":"Lease contests lose real overlaps in three pre-existing cases: same-holder re-claim, more than 8 handovers, a renewal by an undisplayed contestant (fixes bugs B6ac30c2acb, B7164b23643, Bee8e21c547)"},"id":"ee84e9a4d9b1fd5e7b112372c","kind":"task.added","lamport":1799,"schema":1,"subject":"B-fix-contest-gaps","ts":"2026-09-29T09:01:28.811564Z"}
